# kex: check-only
# A `!` function rewrites the `var` it is called on. On a literal or a
# call's result there is none: both backends failed at run time with "'!'
# requires a variable binding as the receiver" (kexhq/kex#770). On a `let`
# it is refused already (KEXET-0425).

main do
  IO.printLine([3, 1].sort!)
  IO.printLine([3, 1].map { |n| n + 1 }.sort!)
  var items = [3, 1]
  items.sort!
  IO.printLine(items)
end
